  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AJE Raising the voice of coastal women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women processors of fishery products face significant climate related challenges to their work including scarcity of resources, loss of production sites, rise in the level of sea /ocean, lack of combustible energy to power the processing ovens, presence of fishmeal factories, etc.


Despite being at the forefront of climate challenges, rural women in Africa, in particular this group of women&#x2019;s voices are underrepresented in climate justice conversations.


Women processors of fish products (fish, oysters, etc.) are naturally included in the initiative. This will largely take place in the coastal zone where there is a high concentration of women who are active in processing and who today are truly impacted by climate change. These women are among the primary actors in the campaign.During this campaign, decision-makers are influenced through the substantial contribution of our community partners (women from rural areas and the coastal strip) to the implementation of the climate agenda of the State of Senegal and Civil Society Organizations.(CSO) for the year 2022. These include, among others, the sustainable mobility and climate week, the African climate week, the Dakclim meetings led by the City of Dakar, the eighteenth session of the African Ministerial Conference on the Environment, the COP27 drum caravan with OxfamSenegal, the series of dialogues between Latin American and African women on the climate crisis and extractive industries. In addition, memoranda will be drawn up, shared with all local authorities (mayors, prefects, governors, prefects, sub-prefects), national (elected chambers, mediator of the republic, economic, social and environmental council) and the technical and financial partners.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Action Justice Environnementale</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">French:
Action pour la Justice Environnementale -AJE est une association cr&#xe9;&#xe9;e par des professionnels des m&#xe9;tiers de l&apos;environnement et qui sont sensibles aux probl&#xe9;matiques contemporaines (changement climatique, d&#xe9;forestation, pollution, inegalites sociales et environnementales etc.)Son objectif principal est de mettre &quot;le droit de l&apos;environnement&quot; entre les mains des communaut&#xe9;s victimes d&apos;injustices environnementales et de faciliter les diff&#xe9;rentes formes de saisine (saisine juridique, non juridique)en cas d&apos;atteinte &#xe0;l&apos;environnement et aux des droits des personnes.

 &#xe0; la formation, la sensibilisation, la cr&#xe9;ation de cadre de concertation et de points focaux (lanceur d&apos;alerte),l&apos;appui &#xe0; la formulation des politiques publiques en mati&#xe8;re environnementale,la recherche et le plaidoyer.

English:
Action for Environmental Justice -AJE is an association created by professionals in the environmental professions who are sensitive to contemporary issues (climate change, deforestation, pollution, socialand environmental inequalities, etc.)
Its main objective is to put &quot;environmental law&quot; in the hands of communities who are victims of environmental injustices and to facilitate the different forms of referral (legal, non-legal referral) in the event ofdamage to the environment and of people&apos;s rights.

to training,
awareness,
the creation of a consultation framework and focal points (whistleblower),support for the formulation of publicpolicies in environmental matters,research and advocacy.</narrative>
